  "id": "fusion-frequency",
  "term": "fusion frequency",
  "definition": "Fusion frequency is the temporal rate at which rapidly alternating visual inputs, such as different colors, are no longer seen as separate events but merge into a single percept. In this context, it refers to the critical frequency beyond which chromatic alternations are perceived as one mixed color.",
